    # normalizes to the seeded email. That is the opposite of
    # the carriage-return username locks: email-validator
    # special-cases CR/LF anywhere with "Carriage return and
    # line feed characters are not allowed" BEFORE any
    # stripping, so CR padding is rejected with 422, while
    # vertical-tab padding is stripped and proceeds. The
    # handler body therefore proceeds, and AuthService.login
    # (auth_service.py) finds the seeded row and runs
    # verify_password with the wrong password, which returns
    # False, raising the same generic UnauthorizedException
    # ("Authentication failed. Please check your credentials.")
    # as the unknown-email, wrong-password, and space-username
